# Next.js App Router Rules (`apps/web/app/*`)

## Version-specific correctness (these break the build if missed)

- `params` and `searchParams` are **always Promises** in this version —
  always `await` them: `const { city, society } = await params`. Never
  destructure or index them synchronously, even in a type that looks
  like a plain object in an older example you might recall.
- Turbopack is the default bundler. Don't add webpack-specific config or
  plugins without checking they have a Turbopack equivalent first.

## Server vs. client components

- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only when a file
  actually needs interactivity (state, effects, browser APIs, event
  handlers) — not preemptively "to be safe."
- Push `"use client"` as far down the tree as possible — wrap just the
  interactive leaf (e.g., the compare-tool widget), not the whole page.
- Data fetching happens in Server Components or Server Actions, not in a
  client-side `useEffect` calling a tRPC procedure that could have run
  server-side.

## Routing & layouts

- Route groups (`(marketplace)`, `(buyer)`, `(society)`, `(dealer)`,
  `(admin)`) map to distinct auth contexts — don't add a page outside its
  intended group, and don't rely on UI-level hiding for access control;
  `middleware.ts` is the actual gate.
- Every new public page under `(marketplace)` implements `generateMetadata`
  — see `seo.mdc` for the full requirement.

## Server Actions

- Validate every Server Action's input with Zod before use, same as a
  tRPC procedure — Server Actions are a public network boundary even
  though they look like local function calls.
- Prefer calling into `packages/api-client` from a Server Action rather
  than duplicating logic — keep one source of truth for a given mutation.

## Images & fonts

- All images via `next/image` with explicit `width`/`height` — no raw
  `<img>` tags, no layout-shift-causing unsized images.
- Fonts via `next/font` only, to avoid FOUT/FOIT and to keep Core Web
  Vitals scores intact on public pages.
